From 0095fb9c9afd0da15152dab3e0974fa9f57b48d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:11:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 125/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: re-check overlays when the
 primary moves or resizes

The overlay atomic_check validates that the overlay rect is contained
in the primary's rect, because the channel window the LAY1..3 layers
ride is anchored to the primary's dst (mbcoor is window-relative).  The
primary's atomic_check pulled the visible overlays into the commit only
when the primary stopped being a valid anchor (AFBC, scaled, or
disabled) - but a commit that merely MOVES or RESIZES a still-valid
primary changes the channel window just the same, and the overlays'
containment check was never re-run against the new geometry.

The staging then clamps the overlay's window-relative coordinate to 0
(sun55i_de_ovl_stage), so after a primary-only move a visible overlay
scanned out at the wrong screen position: the committed DRM state no
longer matched the picture.  No out-of-bounds access is possible (the
fetch is bounded by the overlay's own mbsize/pitch); the bug is purely
a wrong composition.

Pull the visible overlays into the commit whenever the primary's
crtc_x/y/w/h change, forcing their re-check (and an atomic reject if
they no longer fit, so the compositor falls back to GPU composition).
Pure page flips (same geometry) keep the early return and stage no
extra plane state.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
index 9af04eecf..f5fd2b157 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
@@ -376,9 +376,27 @@ static int sun55i_primary_atomic_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	 * overlay is invisible too and its check passes.)
 	 */
 	if (new_state->crtc && fb) {
+		struct drm_plane_state *old_state =
+			drm_atomic_get_old_plane_state(state, plane);
+
 		scaled = (new_state->src_w >> 16) != new_state->crtc_w ||
 			 (new_state->src_h >> 16) != new_state->crtc_h;
-		if (!scaled && fb->modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR)
+		/*
+		 * Still a valid overlay anchor, but the channel window IS the
+		 * primary's dst rect: if this commit moves or resizes it, the
+		 * containment every visible overlay was checked against no
+		 * longer holds, so those overlays must be pulled in and
+		 * re-checked too.  Without this, a primary-only move left the
+		 * overlay's mbcoor clamped against the new window and the
+		 * overlay scanned out at the wrong screen position.  A pure
+		 * page flip (same geometry) still returns early.
+		 */
+		if (!scaled && fb->modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR &&
+		    old_state &&
+		    old_state->crtc_x == new_state->crtc_x &&
+		    old_state->crtc_y == new_state->crtc_y &&
+		    old_state->crtc_w == new_state->crtc_w &&
+		    old_state->crtc_h == new_state->crtc_h)
 			return 0;
 	}
 
